module Main
import Std.Base
import Std.Borrow

-- Regression for the whole-branch review finding on top of the Task-4 clamp
-- fix (08-foreign-lendbuffer-clamp.wok): the REFERENCE interpreter's
-- `Demo.lendBuffer` arm clamped `n` in `Integer` domain (`min n cap`) but had
-- NO `max 0` floor before the single downcast to `Int` (the argument to
-- `Utf8.demoPattern`). For an ordinary negative `n` (like `0 - 1`) this was
-- harmless -- `demoPattern` builds an EMPTY list whenever its `Int` argument
-- is negative, regardless of magnitude. But a literal at or below
-- `-(2^63 + 1)` (a wok `U64` does NOT wrap, so this stays a genuine negative
-- `Integer`) falls outside the representable `Int` range, and the
-- `Integer -> Int` downcast wraps via two's-complement -- landing back in
-- POSITIVE territory for `-(2^63 + 1)` specifically (it wraps to
-- `maxBound :: Int`), so the reference tried to build an astronomically
-- large byte pattern (hang/OOM) while the RC backends -- which already
-- floored at zero -- yielded an empty read. `n` below is exactly that
-- boundary literal, reproducing the divergence pre-fix and the agreed-empty
-- read post-fix on all three backends.
main =
  let n = 0 - 9223372036854775809 in
  length (Demo.lendBuffer n)
